-- Free Quebec vessels from printed pages 79-104 - the Glitter Boy line.
-- Seven rows, and they are the reason this book exists.
--
-- One-off data script, run once per environment. NOT a migration.
--
--   node scripts/d1-apply.mjs --local apps/character-creator/db/zzzzzz-free-quebec-vessels-p079-104.sql
--
-- A VESSEL BELONGS TO THE SLICE ITS NAME HEADING FALLS IN.
--
-- THE CLASSIC GLITTER BOY IS THE USA-G10 and this is the first time it enters
-- the catalog. Before this file the only Glitter Boy vessel here was Triax's
-- T-550, imported with that book; the original the whole line descends from
-- was missing.
--
-- PRINTED 95 HAS A CORRUPT TEXT LAYER AND ONE OF ITS NUMBERS IS WRONG IN THE
-- CACHE - BOOK-INGEST-AUDIT.md F36. The Tarantula's page carries scrambled
-- glyphs ("\Vs. %\%vausttft") in its prose, which is obvious, and TWO damaged
-- figures in its M.D.C. table, which are not: the cache gives the QST-333
-- Shaker Cannon as 115 and the Vibro-Blade as "5Q". Rendered at 200 dpi the
-- page reads 175 and 50. THE FIGURES BELOW ARE THE RENDER'S. An extraction
-- pass over the cached text reported 115 in good faith, which is the whole
-- point of the finding: the tell and the damage are not in the same place.
-- The same render resolved the entry's underwater rule, which is unreadable in
-- the cache: laser range underwater is INCREASED by 50%, while plasma, ion and
-- rail are all halved.
--
-- "RG-IS" IS STORED AS RG-15 AND THE REASON IS INTERNAL. The Classic Glitter
-- Boy's Boom Gun is printed "RG-IS" on printed 82; the Tarantula's optional
-- replacement Boom Gun on printed 97 is printed "RG-15" and points back at the
-- Classic for its stats. Same weapon, and a capital I for a 1 is this corpus's
-- commonest OCR slip. Recorded in the weapon's note rather than silently fixed.
--
-- LASER RESISTANCE IS A LINE-WIDE RULE, not a per-vessel one: every Glitter
-- Boy here takes HALF DAMAGE FROM LASERS, stated generally on printed 84 and
-- repeated in each stat block's main-body footnote. It is on every main body
-- row below, including the Side Kick's, which the book words differently.
--
-- ONLY THE TAURUS REQUIRES A RELOAD TEAM. Printed 78 and printed 98 both say
-- it is always accompanied by one and by a Side Kick, the sole exception being
-- reconnaissance and Special Ops, where it keeps the Side Kick alone. Every
-- other variant mentions Reload Teams as a convenience.
--
-- INSERT OR IGNORE THROUGHOUT, and the readbacks COUNT rather than trusting
-- the exit code.

INSERT OR IGNORE INTO vehicles
  (slug, name, system, vehicle_class, crew, passengers, speed_ground,
   speed_air, speed_water, dimensions, weight_tons, mdc_main_body, cost,
   cost_note, description, source_book)
VALUES
('classic-glitter-boy-qgb-100', 'Classic Glitter Boy (QGB-100 / USA-G10)', 'rifts', 'power-armor', 'One pilot', NULL, 'Running: 60 mph (96 km) maximum, tiring the pilot at only 10% of the normal fatigue rate. Leaping: 12 feet (3.6 m) high or across unassisted, plus 10 feet with a running start; a jet assisted leap reaches 80 feet (24 m) up or across. It can hover up to 12 feet for 1D6x10 seconds.', 'None. The book is explicit: "The thrusters are not made for flying."', 'Swimming 15 mph (24 km or 13 knots); walks the sea floor at about 25% of normal speed. Maximum ocean depth one mile. THE LEG PYLONS MUST BE PLANTED TO FIRE THE BOOM GUN UNDERWATER, or the recoil sends the armor spiralling backward 1D4x100 yards and it loses initiative and its actions.', 'Height: 10 feet 5 inches (3.1 m); Width: 4 feet 4 inches (1.3 m); Length: 4 feet (1.2 m)', '1.2 tons fully loaded', 770, 20000000, 'Free Quebec cost 20 million credits, exclusive to the Free Quebec and NGR military; 15 million without the Boom Gun or the Rimouski Weapon Package. Ancient USA-G10 models and stolen Quebec suits sell on the black market for a minimum of 25 million and sometimes 40 or 50 million. Very rare.', 'The original Glitter Boy: a laser-resistant, one-pilot, ten-foot assault power armor built around the Boom Gun, strong at range and weak up close - which is what the Quebec-designed Rimouski arm package exists to fix for recon, rescue and special-ops suits operating without infantry support. The book calls it both a power armor and a robot in the same paragraph.', 'Rifts World Book 22: Free Quebec p.81-83'),
('triax-glitter-boy-qgb-5-50', 'Triax Glitter Boy (QGB-5-50 "Cyclops")', 'rifts', 'power-armor', 'One', NULL, 'Running: 60 mph (96 km) maximum at 20% of the normal fatigue rate. Leaping: 10 feet (3 m) high, or 15 feet (4.6 m) lengthwise from a running start.', 'None. Printed outright: "Flight is not a capability of the Five-Fifty Cyclops."', 'The book gives this variant no Underwater Capabilities section at all - the only Glitter Boy here without one.', 'Height: 9 feet (2.7 m), or 10 feet (3 m) with the Boom Gun in firing position; Width: 3 feet 9 inches (1.1 m); Length: 4 feet (1.2 m), or 8 feet (2.4 m) nose of gun to back with the weapon deployed', '2 tons', 650, 28000000, 'Free Quebec cost 28 million credits, exclusive to the Free Quebec and NGR military. On the black market this coveted and rare Triax product fetches 60 million.', 'The NGR-built T-550 acquired through the technology-sharing agreement, smaller and sleeker than the Classic and carrying the built-in short-range support weapons the Classic has none of: mini-missiles, an anti-personnel laser and a vibro-sword. The book notes it is reprinted from Rifts World Book Five with text specific to Free Quebec.', 'Rifts World Book 22: Free Quebec p.84-87'),
('glitter-girl-qgb-2-20', 'Glitter Girl (QGB-2-20 "Gigi")', 'rifts', 'power-armor', 'One pilot', NULL, 'Running: 90 mph (145 km) maximum at 10% of the normal fatigue rate. Leaping: 15 feet (4.6 m) high or across unassisted, plus 12 feet with a running start; a jet assisted leap reaches 120 feet (36.5 m) up or across. It can hover up to 18 feet for 2D4x10 seconds.', 'None. "The thrusters are not made for flying."', 'Swimming 20 mph (32 km); walks the bottom at about 25% of normal speed. The pylons must be engaged to fire a Boom Gun when one is fitted. Maximum ocean depth one mile.', 'Height: 9 feet 6 inches (2.9 m); Width: 3 feet 6 inches (1.09 m); Length: 3 feet (0.9 m)', '1 ton fully loaded', 650, 24000000, 'Free Quebec cost 24 million credits, exclusive to the Free Quebec military; 18 million for a suit without any weapon systems.', 'The lighter, faster Glitter Boy flown by the Glitter Girl pilots, armed as standard with the QST-104 "Double-Up" assault cannon rather than a Boom Gun - the Boom Gun is an optional swap for squad leaders and heavy combat. Smaller and quicker than the Classic at the cost of 120 M.D.C.', 'Rifts World Book 22: Free Quebec p.87-91'),
('glitter-boy-side-kick-qpa-98', 'Glitter Boy Side Kick (QPA-98 "Little Buddy")', 'rifts', 'power-armor', 'One', NULL, 'Running: 40 mph (64 km) maximum at 20% of the normal fatigue rate. Leaping: 12 feet (3.6 m) high or lengthwise unassisted; a jet assisted leap from standing reaches 20-60 feet high, averaging 30, and 300 feet across. Sustained bounding travel makes 150 mph (240 km) over ground, reduced 40-50% in dense terrain.', 'Limited flight: maximum altitude 600 feet (183 m), maximum speed 120 mph (192 km), cruising about 60 mph (96.5 km). The jets must cool after an hour of continuous flight - half speed for 3D6 minutes, then they cut out. The nuclear supply lasts a decade; the rockets are the limit.', 'Swimming 25 mph (40 km); walks the bottom at about 25% of normal speed. Maximum depth 1200 feet (366 m). Underwater the grenade launcher loses 25% of its range, the laser pistol GAINS 50%, and other projectile and energy weapons lose half.', 'Height: 7 feet (2.1 m); Width: 3 feet (0.9 m); Length: about 3 feet (0.9 m)', '600 lbs (270 kg) without the jet pack, 1000 lbs (450 kg) with it', 280, 8500000, 'Free Quebec cost 8.5 million credits, largely because of the laser-resistant chrome plating. Exclusive to the Quebec Military and NOT available on the black market, because until the CS war begins its existence is top secret.', 'A man-sized, laser-resistant support power armor with genuine flight, assigned roughly one per two to four Glitter Boys to scout, screen and help reload. It is the exception in the line: no weapon is built into it, and everything it carries is hand-held.', 'Rifts World Book 22: Free Quebec p.92-94'),
('tarantula-glitter-boy-qgb-3-30', 'Tarantula Glitter Boy (QGB-3-30 "T-Boy")', 'rifts', 'power-armor', 'One pilot', NULL, 'Running: 50 mph (80 km) maximum at 10% of the normal fatigue rate. Leaping: 10 feet (3 m) high or across, plus 10 feet with a running start; a jet assisted leap reaches 60 feet (18 m) up or across. It can hover 10 feet for 1D6x10 seconds. Physical strength is equal to a P.S. of 40.', 'None stated.', 'Swimming 15 mph (24 km or 13 knots); walks the bottom at about 25% of normal walking and running speed. Maximum ocean depth 1.2 miles (1.9 km). UNDERWATER, LASER RANGE IS INCREASED BY 50% while the range of the plasma, ion and rail weapons is all reduced by half - read off a 200 dpi render, because this passage is unreadable in the cached text.', 'Height: 11 feet 5 inches (3.4 m) head to toe, plus 3 feet (0.9 m) for the pair of large back fins; Width: 4 feet 8 inches (1.46 m); Length: 4 feet 6 inches (1.4 m)', '1.6 tons fully loaded', 850, 23000000, 'Free Quebec cost 23 million credits, exclusive to the Free Quebec and NGR military; 19 million without the QST-333 or other weapon features. Not available on the black market because until the CS war begins its existence is top secret. Future black market models are likely to fetch a minimum of 30 million and as much as 50; very rare.', 'The biggest of the Glitter Boy line: a restyled, heavier Classic using stabilising fins instead of ground pylons, built to carry the experimental triple-mode "Shaker" cannon in place of the Boom Gun. Its designer named it for the way the many small fins resemble a tarantula''s hairs and the pair of large fins its outstretched legs.', 'Rifts World Book 22: Free Quebec p.95-97'),
('taurus-glitter-boy-qgb-7-70', 'Taurus Glitter Boy (QGB-7-70 "Two-Guns")', 'rifts', 'power-armor', 'One pilot', 'None, though it is always accompanied by a Reload Team and a Side Kick.', 'Running: 50 mph (80 km) maximum at 10% of the normal fatigue rate. Leaping: 8 feet (2.4 m) high or across, plus 10 feet with a running start; a jet assisted leap reaches 60 feet (18 m) up or across. It can hover 12 feet for 1D6x10 seconds.', 'None stated.', 'Swimming 15 mph (24 km or 13 knots); walks the bottom at about 25% of normal speed. Weapon range underwater is reduced by about half, mortars included, and firing recoil underwater propels the armor at least 100 yards. Maximum ocean depth one mile.', 'Height: 10 feet 10 inches (3.3 m), plus 3 feet (0.9 m) with the shoulder weapons mounted; Width: 4 feet 4 inches (1.3 m), plus 4 feet (1.2 m) with the guns; Length: 4 feet (1.2 m), plus 3 feet (0.9 m) with the guns', '1 ton base, 2 tons fully loaded', 800, 18000000, 'Free Quebec cost 18 million credits WITHOUT WEAPONS - the only price in this book stated that way, so the figure is not comparable with the other variants'' fully-equipped prices. Exclusive to the Free Quebec and NGR military. A fully loaded Taurus on the black market would command something in the range of 30-45 million. Very rare.', 'The artillery Glitter Boy: rare, at about 5% of the force, mortar or laser-cannon armed, and deliberately shaped to look like an ordinary Glitter Boy in formation so it does not draw counter-battery fire. Alone in the line it is designed never to operate alone - a Reload Team works the big guns while a Side Kick defends both.', 'Rifts World Book 22: Free Quebec p.98-100'),
('silver-wolf-glitter-boy-qgb-8-88', 'Silver Wolf Glitter Boy (QGB-8-88 "Wolf")', 'rifts', 'power-armor', 'One pilot', NULL, 'Running: 90 mph (145 km) maximum at 10% of the normal fatigue rate. Leaping: 15 feet (4.6 m) high or across, plus 12 feet with a running start; a jet assisted leap reaches 120 feet (36.5 m) up or across. It can hover 18 feet for 2D4x10 seconds.', 'None stated.', 'Swimming 25 mph (40 km); walks the bottom at about 25% of normal speed. Maximum depth 3000 feet (914 m). Firing the particle beam underwater superheats the water and makes the armor an easy target for heat sensors, and cuts the P-Beam''s range by 75%, to 500 feet; laser range drops by half, mini-missiles by a quarter, and other weapons by half.', 'Height: 8 feet (2.4 m); Width: 3 feet 3 inches (1.06 m); Length: 3 feet (0.9 m), not counting the roughly 6 feet 7 inch (2.04 m) particle beam cannon', '1400 lbs (630 kg) fully loaded', 450, 20000000, 'Free Quebec cost 20 million credits, exclusive to the Free Quebec military; 15.4 million for a suit without any weapon systems.', 'A smaller, faster covert-operations Glitter Boy built around a particle beam cannon it can fire kneeling, prone, or slung across its own back - it needs no pylons, which is what lets it shoot from cover. Deployed in "Wolf Pack" squads of six to ten on sabotage, assassination and reconnaissance rather than in mass formations.', 'Rifts World Book 22: Free Quebec p.101-104');

